module insd-criminal-local-rules.local-rules

import core.frcrimp45.{ frcrimp45 }

// The Southern District of Indiana's own criminal periods, counted under
// the criminal rules (FRCrimP 45(a) governs "any local rule"). No trigger
// carries a service method: FRCrimP 45(c)'s three added days follow the
// manner of service, which is not modeled here.
//
// Periods that are FRCrimP periods stay in lit/frcrimp and are only named
// here: objections or corrections to the presentence report within 14
// days following its disclosure, unless the court determines otherwise
// (S.D. Ind. L. Cr. R. 32-2(e); FRCrimP 32(f)(1)), and the report with its
// addendum to the sentencing judge no later than 7 days before the
// sentencing date (L. Cr. R. 32-2(g); FRCrimP 32(g)). The report is
// deemed disclosed when electronically served on counsel through CM/ECF
// (L. Cr. R. 32-2(d)).
//
// A motion to quash a grand-jury subpoena is due no later than 48 hours
// before the appearance or production date unless good cause exists for a
// later filing (L. Cr. R. 6-1(c)(2)); lit/core's FRCrimP 45(a) rule counts
// days, so the 48 hours stay in this note. A non-exempt party filing a
// document with the clerk presents it within 1 business day after filing
// the notice of manual filing (L. Cr. R. 49-1(e)(2)), a business-day
// period also kept in this note.
//
// Conditions that are not deadlines from an event stay in notes: the court
// may issue a standard order served with the indictment or information
// (L. Cr. R. 7-1), not vendored; a continuance motion sets out its
// conformity with the Speedy Trial Act with a proposed entry (L. Cr. R.
// 12-1); the sentencing hearing is scheduled after a plea petition, plea
// agreement, guilty plea or verdict (L. Cr. R. 32-2(a)); a motion to keep
// a case sealed is filed no later than the initial appearance (L. Cr. R.
// 49.1-2(a)); an opposition to a motion to maintain under seal runs under
// S.D. Ind. L.R. 7-1 from the filing of the brief in support (L. Cr. R.
// 49.1-2(i)), a civil period that stays in lit/insd. Petitions under 28
// U.S.C. §§ 2241, 2254 and 2255 and capital challenges (L. Cr. R. 38-1,
// 38-2) belong to federal habeas (lit/habeas) and are not encoded here.
//
// The earlier S.D. Ind. criminal outline's FRCrimP flow and its decisions
// are FRCrimP, Speedy Trial Act or constitutional authority and belong to
// lit/frcrimp; they are removed here: no reporter text is vendored.
/// A brief in support of a motion to maintain a case or document under
/// seal: at most 10 pages (S.D. Ind. L. Cr. R. 49.1-2(h)).
limit seal-brief {
  pages <= 10 cite "S.D. Ind. L. Cr. R. 49.1-2(h)"
} cite "S.D. Ind. L. Cr. R. 49.1-2(h)"

/// A brief in opposition to a motion to maintain a case or document under
/// seal: at most 10 pages (S.D. Ind. L. Cr. R. 49.1-2(i)).
limit seal-opposition-brief {
  pages <= 10 cite "S.D. Ind. L. Cr. R. 49.1-2(i)"
} cite "S.D. Ind. L. Cr. R. 49.1-2(i)"

/// A motion to reassign a criminal case as related is filed (S.D. Ind. L.
/// Cr. R. 12-2(b)).
event ReassignmentMotionFiled()
/// A petition to enter a plea of guilty or a plea agreement is filed, a
/// guilty plea is entered, or a guilty verdict is returned (S.D. Ind. L.
/// Cr. R. 32-2(a), (c)).
event SentencingProcessCommenced()
/// A Motion to Maintain Document(s) Under Seal identifying another party as
/// the designating party is served (S.D. Ind. L. Cr. R. 49.1-2(g)).
event SealMotionServed()
/// A brief in support of a motion to maintain under seal is filed (S.D.
/// Ind. L. Cr. R. 49.1-2(h), (i)).
event SealBriefFiled() paper seal-brief
/// A brief in opposition to a motion to maintain under seal is filed (S.D.
/// Ind. L. Cr. R. 49.1-2(i)).
event SealOppositionFiled() paper seal-opposition-brief
/// An order denying a motion to maintain a case or document under seal is
/// served (S.D. Ind. L. Cr. R. 49.1-2(a), (j)).
event SealDenialServed()

/// S.D. Ind. L. Cr. R. 12-2(b): any objection to a motion to reassign a
/// criminal case as related is filed within 7 days of the filing of the
/// motion.
deadline reassignment-objection: 7.days after ReassignmentMotionFiled() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "S.D. Ind. L. Cr. R. 12-2(b)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// S.D. Ind. L. Cr. R. 32-2(c): within 14 days after a plea petition, plea
/// agreement, guilty plea or guilty verdict, government and defense counsel
/// each submit in writing their version of the facts of the offense to the
/// probation officer, or notify the officer that it is captured in a
/// document already available, providing it to the other party first or
/// at the same time.
deadline offense-versions: 14.days after SentencingProcessCommenced() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "S.D. Ind. L. Cr. R. 32-2(c)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// S.D. Ind. L. Cr. R. 49.1-2(g)(2): the designating party files a
/// Statement Authorizing Unsealing or a Brief in Support within 14 days of
/// service of the Motion to Maintain Document(s) Under Seal; if it does
/// not, the court may rule summarily.
deadline designating-party-statement: 14.days after SealMotionServed() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "S.D. Ind. L. Cr. R. 49.1-2(g)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// S.D. Ind. L. Cr. R. 49.1-2(a), (j): after the court denies a motion to
/// maintain a case or document under seal, the clerk unseals it 21 days
/// after service of the order, absent a FRCrimP 59(a) objection, a motion
/// to reconsider, notice of an intended interlocutory appeal or a further
/// order; a party acts within the 21 days to keep the seal.
deadline unseal-after-denial: 21.days after SealDenialServed() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "S.D. Ind. L. Cr. R. 49.1-2(j); S.D. Ind. L. Cr. R. 49.1-2(a)"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

test "reassignment objection: 7 days after the trigger" cite "S.D. Ind. L. Cr. R. 12-2(b)"
{
  given ReassignmentMotionFiled() on 2027-03-01
  expect deadline(reassignment-objection) == 2027-03-08
}

test "offense versions: 14 days after the trigger" cite "S.D. Ind. L. Cr. R. 32-2(c)"
{
  given SentencingProcessCommenced() on 2027-03-01
  expect deadline(offense-versions) == 2027-03-15
}

test "designating party statement: 14 days after the trigger" cite "S.D. Ind. L. Cr. R. 49.1-2(g)"
{
  given SealMotionServed() on 2027-03-01
  expect deadline(designating-party-statement) == 2027-03-15
}

test "unseal after denial: 21 days after the trigger" cite "S.D. Ind. L. Cr. R. 49.1-2(j); S.D. Ind. L. Cr. R. 49.1-2(a)"
{
  given SealDenialServed() on 2027-03-01
  expect deadline(unseal-after-denial) == 2027-03-22
}
